config ZEPHYR_OSAL
    default n
    bool "openbmc zephyr OS adapter layer"

config SHELL_MEMTESTER
    bool "shell memtester tool"

config OPENBMC_IPMI_LAT
    bool "IPMI request latency probe (RAM ring + ipmi_lat shell command)"
    default n
    depends on SHELL
    help
      Records k_uptime_ticks() at ten points of every IPMI request/response
      cycle (net-ipmid receive, D-Bus hand-off, the two moments dbus-broker
      dequeues and forwards each message, ipmid entry/exit, D-Bus reply,
      datagram sent) into a 128-entry RAM ring, and exposes them as
      "ipmi_lat dump" / "ipmi_lat clear".

      Nothing is printed on the hot path on purpose: one IPMI request already
      spends ~33 ms blocking in UART output at 115200 baud (the two ipmid
      traces plus the DBG line), so printk-based instrumentation would measure
      itself. With this disabled the probe call sites compile to nothing.

      The implementation lives in this module (src/ipmi_lat.c) rather than in
      the application so that every branch sharing zephyr-osal links the probe
      symbols declared by sdbusplus, basu and dbus-broker, even when it does
      not pick up the application's changes.
